    "offices": {
      "President": "Elected by popular vote for a four-year term, renewable once in a row; a candidate needs more than half of all ballots cast, otherwise the top two meet in a run-off. The Guardian Council must approve every candidate, and the president, who heads the government, ranks below the Supreme Leader.",
      "Parliament": "The Islamic Consultative Assembly (Majlis) has 290 members elected for four years in single- and multi-member constituencies, five of them in seats reserved for religious minorities; a candidate needs a quarter of the votes to win in the first round, otherwise a run-off is held. The Guardian Council approves all candidates and the laws the Majlis passes."
